{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on 5d56adca: registration admission before O4.\n\nO4 opens no dynamic registration. Claude and ChatGPT both identify\nthemselves with client ID metadata documents from origins on\nOAUTH_CLIENT_METADATA_ORIGINS, so the witness needs no POST\n/oauth/register. Closing it removes the anonymous refill entirely, with\nno rate limit to tune.\n\n1. A small source change, filed as its own request after this act:\n   OAUTH_DYNAMIC_REGISTRATION, off by default. When off, POST\n   /oauth/register refuses with a fixed error and records nothing, and\n   the authorization-server metadata omits registration_endpoint. When\n   \"on\", today's behavior holds. An invalid value closes the OAuth\n   routes. O4's Worker runs with it off.\n2. Anonymous refill: accepted as residual risk only for a Worker with\n   registration on. Before any Worker turns it on, for Goose or\n   Gemini, a per-address rate limit on POST /oauth/register lands\n   first. I file that when it is next.\n3. Member-protected capacity: accepted for the O4 witness. The\n   dedicated Worker's rooms hold only witness members. Every consent\n   is a Native act signed by a member, so a member who fills the\n   protected slots is identifiable. Revisit before any Worker serves\n   people outside the project.\n4. Hosted MCP on O4's Worker opens only for the live runs, in a window\n   I name, as with J1. It closes afterwards.\n\nBuilder: please ratify this report by its own ID so 5d56adca closes.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8e451d33d78bd38d571001b4ea5871e62147cbbb stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d3d93d0754c6a3eeae515f3c3dc0c10b30d972d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0f403e804f9757ee6c0664ea9757b53711be3991, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:16d4bcf17e223194b265c810a331c1b9265345b9, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f